<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Q:<sp/>**_&quot;We<sp/>should<sp/>be<sp/>able<sp/>to<sp/>deal<sp/>with<sp/>the<sp/>fact<sp/>that<sp/>MiniLibX<sp/>is<sp/>not<sp/>perfect,<sp/>it<sp/>is<sp/>by<sp/>design<sp/>and<sp/>makes<sp/>us<sp/>better<sp/>programmers.&quot;_**</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">A:<sp/>Struggle<sp/>does<sp/>bring<sp/>out<sp/>the<sp/>best<sp/>in<sp/>most<sp/>people<sp/>but<sp/>it<sp/>is<sp/>also<sp/>not<sp/>ideal<sp/>in<sp/>this<sp/>case.<sp/>I<sp/>think<sp/>so<sp/>at<sp/>least,<sp/>that<sp/>it&apos;s<sp/>really<sp/>expected<sp/>that<sp/>libraries<sp/>that<sp/>are<sp/>publicly<sp/>available<sp/>should<sp/>be<sp/>usable,<sp/>stable,<sp/>easy<sp/>to<sp/>use<sp/>and<sp/>well<sp/>documented.<sp/>Nobody<sp/>uses<sp/>a<sp/>library<sp/>because<sp/>it<sp/>is<sp/>annoying<sp/>to<sp/>work<sp/>with<sp/>and<sp/>afterwards<sp/>think<sp/>to<sp/>themselves<sp/>they<sp/>have<sp/>learned<sp/>something<sp/>after<sp/>they<sp/>are<sp/>done<sp/>struggling.<sp/>The<sp/>only<sp/>thing<sp/>people<sp/>learn<sp/>from<sp/>this<sp/>is<sp/>how<sp/>to<sp/>navigate<sp/>around<sp/>the<sp/>shortcomings<sp/>instead.</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Q:<sp/>**_&quot;Why<sp/>not<sp/>use<sp/>some<sp/>other<sp/>library?<sp/>Why<sp/>this<sp/>one<sp/>and<sp/>not<sp/>any<sp/>other<sp/>library.&quot;_**</highlight></codeline>
